.TH LIBPUCI 3 "November 2026" "puci 0.6.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
libpuci \- embeddable AI agent loop for C programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <puci/puci.h>
.PP
.BI "puci_status puci_context_create(const puci_context_options *" opts ", puci_context **" out );
.BI "puci_status puci_context_set_provider(puci_context *" ctx ", const puci_provider_config *" cfg );
.BI "puci_status puci_session_create(const puci_context *" ctx ", const puci_session_options *" opts ", puci_session **" out );
.BI "puci_status puci_session_send(puci_session *" s ", const char *" message );
.BI "void puci_session_destroy(puci_session *" s );
.BI "void puci_context_destroy(puci_context *" ctx );
.fi
.PP
Compile and link with
.BR "pkg\-config \-\-cflags \-\-libs puci" .
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libpuci
runs the model / tool loop of a coding agent inside your program.
A
.I context
holds the provider and the registered tools; a
.I session
is one conversation.
.BR puci_session_send ()
runs a whole turn and reports progress through the
.I event_cb
in
.IR puci_session_options .
.PP
For programs with their own event loop, the turn can be driven without
blocking:
.BR puci_session_begin_turn (),
.BR puci_session_get_fds (),
.BR puci_session_next_timeout_ms (),
.BR puci_session_process ()
and
.BR puci_session_next_event ().
Many sessions can share one
.BR poll (2)
loop.
.SH TOOLS
Built in: read_file, write_file, edit_file, grep, glob and run_shell.
Add your own with
.BR puci_tool_register ()
or, for long\-running work,
.BR puci_tool_register_async ().
MCP servers are attached with
.BR puci_mcp_server_register ().
.SH SAFETY
Without an
.I approve_cb
(or
.I approval_mode
= PUCI_APPROVAL_MODE_EVENT), only read_file, grep and glob run; every other
tool is denied. Set
.I approval_mode
= PUCI_APPROVAL_MODE_AUTO to run everything unattended.
Set
.I workspace_root
to confine the file tools to a directory.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Functions return PUCI_OK (0) on success or a nonzero
.IR puci_status ;
.BR puci_status_string ()
names it and
.BR puci_session_error ()
gives details.
.SH EXAMPLE
See
.I examples/minimal_agent.c
in the source distribution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR puci (1)
.PP
Headers in
.I <puci/*.h>
document every function.
